From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rdkb-cli: release native response-tree allocations

The WebUI has a second ownership boundary: exec() returns a newly allocated C
network tree. Live topology and configuration handlers never released most
returned trees, and traversal helpers leaked every temporary CString key.
Because the topology page polls once per minute, this eventually OOM-killed
onewifi_em_cli in the 1 GiB controller container.

Bound temporary CString ownership, free command result trees (including
set-command replies), and close two smaller error/update path leaks in the CLI
C++ layer.

---
